## Starting pattern

`INV-\d{4}-\d{6}`

It fails three lines: it accepts any four-digit year, and it does not allow the branch suffix.

data cases = line,expected,actual,verdict; `INV-2026-004711`,Valid,Valid,Passed; `INV-2025-000032`,Valid,Valid,Passed; `INV-2026-104711`,Valid,Valid,Passed; `INV-2026-004711/B2`,Valid,Not valid,Failed; `INV-2026-004711/NY`,Valid,Not valid,Failed; `inv-2026-004711` (lowercase),Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV-2023-004711` (year too old),Not valid,Valid,Failed; `INV-2026-4711` (sequence too short),Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV-2026-0047112` (too long),Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV-2026-004711/b2`,Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV-2026-004711` plus a trailing space,Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `Ref: INV-2026-004711`,Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV 2026 004711`,Not valid,Not valid,Passed

table cases title="Starting pattern, line by line"

## Suggested pattern

`^INV-(?:2024|2025|2026)-\d{6}(?:/(?:B\d|[A-Z]{2}))?$`

- `^` and `$` anchor the whole line, which rejects the prefix, the trailing space and the 7-digit sequence.
- `(?:2024|2025|2026)` limits the year to 2024 to 2026.
- `\d{6}` needs exactly six digits.
- `(?:/(?:B\d|[A-Z]{2}))?` allows an optional branch suffix, either B and a digit (B2) or two capital letters (NY). Lowercase /b2 is rejected.

! The suffix rule is a guess from two examples. If branches can be other shapes, say so and widen it; if only /B2 and /NY exist, `/(?:B2|NY)` is stricter.

table = line,expected,actual,verdict; `INV-2026-004711`,Valid,Valid,Passed; `INV-2025-000032`,Valid,Valid,Passed; `INV-2026-104711`,Valid,Valid,Passed; `INV-2026-004711/B2`,Valid,Valid,Passed; `INV-2026-004711/NY`,Valid,Valid,Passed; `inv-2026-004711`,Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV-2023-004711`,Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV-2026-4711`,Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV-2026-0047112`,Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV-2026-004711/b2`,Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV-2026-004711` plus a trailing space,Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `Ref: INV-2026-004711`,Not valid,Not valid,Passed; `INV 2026 004711`,Not valid,Not valid,Passed

## Slow patterns

The suggested pattern is safe on long text: it has no nested or repeated groups, so it cannot backtrack catastrophically. Watch for shapes like `(\d+)+`, `(a|aa)*` or `(.*)*`, where a repeated group contains something that can match the same text in several ways. They can freeze a validator on a long non-matching line.

## Copy

```
^INV-(?:2024|2025|2026)-\d{6}(?:/(?:B\d|[A-Z]{2}))?$
```
